B11 (task 6.2; wiki/site/gate-a-open-items.md §3 working default "three new events, no database change", confirmed by
  the main session 2026-10-14; architecture §8.2; ADR-013 "The B11 checkout events"): two new events, to GA4 and
  PostHog only, through the dispatcher src/lib/tracking/track.ts (never Meta). Measurement only:
  - `preorder_payment_failed { tier, reason_code, reason }`: `checkout.on("payment.failed", ...)` registered BEFORE
    `open()`, as Razorpay requires. Only `error.code` and `error.reason` are read, and only when each has Razorpay's
    documented shape, words joined by underscores, at most 64 characters: upper case for the code (BAD_REQUEST_ERROR),
    lower case for the reason (payment_failed). Anything else, a bare number or a single word included (it could be a
    phone number or a name; review of 6.2), is sent as "unknown". `error.description` (free text), `error.source`,
    `error.step` and `error.metadata` (the gateway's order and payment ids) are never read.
  - `preorder_payment_window_opened { tier }`: right after `checkout.open()`.
  - `tier` joins StartCheckoutInput for these two events only. It is NOT passed to Razorpay: the options object,
    `handler`, `modal.ondismiss`, the one `open()` and the boolean answer are the tag's (test/checkout-events.test.tsx
    runs the tag's checkout.ts beside this one and compares what Razorpay is handed).
  - `measure()` swallows a throw from a measuring tool, so no tool can change the payment path or the answer.
  - `RazorpayInstance.on` is typed for the one event used; still optional, still called with `?.`.
  Nothing else changes: the script URL, loading, the amount (from create-order), the key, notes, theme #EF762F.

